37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings reveal a clear pattern: projects with shared accessibility are rated highest, while those benefiting only a single wing are viewed as disappointments. Additionally, hazardous materials in older blocks are causing significant delays.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings indicate a significant imbalance; specialist rooms are often idle, while general-purpose rooms are overcapacity. Furthermore, taking rooms out of service has forced us to pay for expensive off-site hired space.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are all uncovering the same tragedy from different angles. My records show that while basic surfacing remains stable, mechanical costs are surging, and projects driven by ""appeal"" systematically slip by a year or more.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, you're right, Benjamin! I found out that mechanical and plant costs are way up—like a fifth higher! Plus, we're writing off AV gear but have no money saved to replace it. The numbers on paper are totally wrong!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we've all found our respective disasters. My data shows that while some new hires have spare time, our bench technicians are wasting hours on manual routines because our equipment is outdated. We're essentially paying people to be human substitutes for machines.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that is a distressing realization. It seems we are facing a systemic failure where our infrastructure is not only outdated but is actively hindering the people who maintain it. We must prioritize efficiency over aesthetics.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. However, we must also consider the operational cost of the transition. If we prioritize general-purpose spaces, we need a plan that doesn't force us into costly off-site rentals during construction.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a most pertinent concern. It would be a charming irony to solve our capacity crisis by spending our remaining budget on temporary rentals. We must seek a path that avoids such administrative gymnastics.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that does sound like a mess! But if we don't fix the equipment and the budget gaps now, won't we just keep spending more money later? We need a plan that's actually honest about the costs!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, honesty is a rare commodity in these halls. While you're worried about the budget gaps, I'm looking at the people filling them with their own time. We can't just ""be honest"" about costs; we need to stop the manual drudgery.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I agree. The human cost of manual drudgery is a debt we cannot ignore. We need a solution that provides shared utility and operational relief without risking the delays found in the older blocks.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. However, we must ensure that any ""operational relief"" doesn't come at the cost of our timetable. If a project requires taking essential rooms out of service, the resulting disruption could be counterproductive.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, your caution is well-placed. We must avoid the seductive trap of a ""perfect"" solution that requires a year of chaos to implement. A plan that slips into the next term is not a plan; it is a gamble.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I don't want to gamble either! But if we just pick the ""safe"" option and ignore that costs are rising and AV gear is breaking, aren't we just gambling with the future? We need a plan that's realistic!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, realism isn't just about the price of a screen or a pipe. It's about whether the people left standing can actually handle the workload. A ""safe"" plan that ignores staff burnout is just a slow-motion failure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It is clear we are all describing a fragile system. We need a candidate that maximizes shared utility and reduces staff burden, while avoiding the hazardous materials of the older blocks and the instability of ""appeal"" projects.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We must find a balance where the long-term utility of the space is achieved without creating an immediate crisis in our timetable or our budget for off-site rentals. Predictability is as important as the result.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. Predictability is the only antidote to the chronic optimism that plagues our planning. We must favor a project that is a necessity rather than a luxury, as the records suggest only the former actually arrive on time.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I totally agree! Let's look for a project that's a real necessity and doesn't pretend that costs stay the same. If we pick something honest and useful, we can actually make it happen!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's hope the candidates are actually honest for once. I'll be looking for a plan that treats our technicians like professionals rather than manual labor. If it doesn't reduce the drudgery, it's just more noise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
