60,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, Plan D is the most responsible choice. It provides shared utility and directly addresses the operational drudgery Shunichi mentioned, while avoiding the hazardous materials of the older blocks found in Plan A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Plan D is a necessary upgrade, but we must be cautious. Replacing ventilation in shared labs likely requires taking them out of service, which could lead to the expensive off-site rentals I discovered in the records.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a valid concern, though perhaps a necessary evil. However, Plan D is a functional necessity, not a project of ""appeal."" According to the records, such essential works are the only ones that actually respect our calendars.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree! Plan D sounds like a real necessity. Plus, since I saw that mechanical costs are way up, it's better to fix the ventilation now than to pretend it's cheap and get a surprise bill later!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Plan D is the only option that isn't a vanity project. It actually solves the problem of our technicians acting as human ventilation switches. If we can manage the timetable, it's the only choice that makes sense.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, if we schedule the ventilation work during the summer break, we can mitigate the rental costs. Given the consensus on operational relief and shared utility, Plan D is the most robust and honest choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, summer scheduling is a possibility, but we must ensure the scope doesn't bleed into the term. If we can guarantee the timetable remains intact, Plan D's utility and operational benefits make it the most rational choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, your insistence on a strict schedule is the only thing standing between us and another year of administrative chaos. If we commit to a summer window, Plan D becomes a triumph of pragmatism over optimism.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Victoria, I'm with you! If we can just be super strict about the summer schedule, it'll be great. Plan D is the most honest choice because it deals with the real stuff that's actually getting more expensive!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, your caution is noted, but let's be honest: the current situation is already a crisis for the staff. A few weeks of scheduling stress is a fair trade for ending years of manual drudgery. I vote for Plan D.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree with Shunichi. The long-term benefit of shared utility and staff relief far outweighs the temporary scheduling risk. Plan D is the only candidate that aligns with all our findings. I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. While I remain cautious about the timetable, the collective benefits for staff and students outweigh the risks, provided we manage the schedule strictly. I also vote for Plan D.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare and satisfying thing to see such alignment. Plan D avoids the pitfalls of ""appeal"" and addresses a functional necessity, making it the only candidate likely to survive the calendar. I vote for Plan D.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm totally on board! Plan D is the only one that doesn't ignore the real costs of mechanical work, and it helps the staff too. It's the most honest and useful plan! I vote for Plan D!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we've reached a consensus with surprising speed. Plan D is the only option that treats our infrastructure and our people with a modicum of respect. I cast my vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It is a relief to reach this conclusion together. By prioritizing shared utility and the well-being of our staff over superficial appeal, we have made a decision that is both logical and compassionate. I cast my final vote for Plan D.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am satisfied that we have balanced the need for operational relief with a commitment to timetable stability. By choosing a necessary upgrade, we ensure a sustainable future for our facilities. I cast my final vote for Plan D.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,The evidence has spoken with an unusual degree of clarity. Plan D is the only option that balances operational necessity with financial realism and a predictable timeline. I cast my final vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! Picking Plan D means we're finally being honest about the costs and actually helping the people who work here. I cast my final vote for Plan D!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm satisfied. We've managed to avoid the usual vanity projects and actually address the systemic failure of our equipment. It's a rare win for the people actually doing the work. I cast my final vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
